  <name xml:lang="en">One Company, End to End (starter)</name>
  <documentation xml:lang="en">A small subscription business modelled end to end: what it is trying to achieve, the capabilities that deliver it, the applications behind them, the suppliers and contracts behind those, what each costs, who owns it and what could go wrong. Because every piece is connected, the model answers the questions people actually ask: what breaks if a system or supplier fails, what a capability really costs, and who has to act. Replace the example company with your own, starting from a spreadsheet of applications.</documentation>
